  "track.arch.cap.offline": "Left to right: screen, repository, database; the network below. Dots moving against an arrow are data going up. A red-outlined box holds or shows a stale copy; a hatched box is the network being unavailable.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s1.title": "Open the screen: show yesterday's saved copy",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s1.explain": "The repository returns a Flow from the database; the screen shows 9:00 and 9:30 as free, per yesterday's copy.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.mixed.s1": "Open the screen: show yesterday's saved copy",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s2.title": "Pull to refresh: the network result goes straight to the UI",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s2.explain": "The server returns a new copy: 9:30 is now taken. refresh() hands this list to the ViewModel, which puts it in state. The UI is right, but the database was never written.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.mixed.s2": "Pull to refresh: the network result goes straight to the UI",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s3.title": "Reopen the screen: 9:30 shows as free again",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s3.explain": "The next time it opens, or any other screen reading the database, still sees yesterday's copy. The user picks 9:30 and gets \"this slot is taken\".",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.mixed.s3": "Reopen the screen: 9:30 shows as free again",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s4.title": "Offline: only the old copy is left",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.mixed.s4.explain": "Offline, the refresh fails, and the database never received the new copy. The app can still read, but it reads data older than what the user has already seen.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.mixed.s4": "Offline: only the old copy is left",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s1.title": "Open the screen: the UI observes the database",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s1.explain": "The repository has a single read function: a Flow from the database. The ViewModel turns it into a StateFlow; the screen shows the saved copy.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.ssot.s1": "Open the screen: the UI observes the database",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s2.title": "Refresh: the network only writes into the database",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s2.explain": "refresh() downloads the new list and writes it into the database. It returns nothing to the UI; the UI has not changed yet at this step.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.ssot.s2": "Refresh: the network only writes into the database",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s3.title": "The database emits again: every screen sees the new copy",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s3.explain": "The free-slot table changed, so the Flow emits the new list; Choose a time and every other observing screen update together. The next open sees the new copy too, because it is in the database.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.ssot.s3": "The database emits again: every screen sees the new copy",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s4.title": "Offline: still reads the latest saved copy",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.ssot.s4.explain": "The refresh throws; the repository reports that error separately (\"you are offline\") and does not wipe data. The screen still shows the latest saved copy.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.ssot.s4": "Offline: still reads the latest saved copy",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s1.title": "Cancel while offline: write the database first",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s1.explain": "The user taps Cancel on the 10:00 appointment. The repository marks it cancelled in the database, with a \"pending sync\" flag.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.lazy.s1": "Cancel while offline: write the database first",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s2.title": "The UI updates at once, still offline",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s2.explain": "The database changed, so the Flow emits again; the screen shows \"cancelled (pending sync)\". The user does not wait for the network.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.lazy.s2": "The UI updates at once, still offline",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s3.title": "Queue the sync with WorkManager",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s3.explain": "The repository enqueues a unique \"sync-cancel-<id>\" job that runs only when online. The job survives the app being closed or the device restarting.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.lazy.s3": "Queue the sync with WorkManager",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s4.title": "Back online: push to the server, clear the pending flag",
  "track.arch.m.offline.s.lazy.s4.explain": "WorkManager runs the worker: it calls api.cancel(id); on success it clears the pending flag in the database, on failure it retries later. The UI changes to \"cancelled\".",
  "track.arch.m.offline.ev.lazy.s4": "Back online: push to the server, clear the pending flag",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.try": "Walk the four steps of each approach; compare \"The UI has the latest copy\" with \"The DB has the latest copy\".",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.mixed.s2": "Offline-first: repository reads come straight from the local data source; every update is written there first so it notifies its readers. Both are skipped here. [[src:ax-offline-first]]",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.mixed.s3": "The local data source must be the only place higher layers read from, to keep data consistent across connection states. [[src:ax-offline-first]]",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.mixed.s4": "At a minimum an offline-first app must be able to read without network; this app can, but it reads the stale copy.",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.ssot.s2": "The repository can only notify its readers of changes by updating its local data source first. [[src:ax-offline-first]]",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.ssot.s3": "Reads use observable types (Flow) so new data shows as soon as it arrives; the ViewModel turns the Flow into a StateFlow with stateIn. [[src:ax-offline-first]]",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.ssot.s4": "Network read errors are handled separately (retry with exponential backoff, or wait for connectivity); local data keeps showing. [[src:ax-offline-first]]",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.lazy.s2": "Lazy writes: write to the local data source first, then queue the write to notify the network as soon as feasible. [[src:ax-offline-first]]",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.lazy.s3": "Draining an offline write queue is persistent work, usually delegated to WorkManager. [[src:ax-offline-first]]",
  "track.arch.m.offline.co.lazy.s4": "When the device and the server both change the same data, conflicts must be resolved; that belongs to the System Design track (i8).",
  "track.arch.preset.offline": "Architecture · the database as the source of truth (offline-first)",
